{"game_id":2026020375,"away":"EDM","home":"STL","split":{"name":"Jones","side":0,"sec":2729},"lede":"St. Louis had last change, so Jim Montgomery picked most of these matchups. St. Louis played without Connor McMichael and Ross Johnston. Edmonton played without Ty Emberson and Zach Hyman and lost Max Jones after 5:29 of the third.","notes":[{"kind":"match","head":"Thomas’s line drew McDavid’s line","text":"Jim Montgomery sent Neighbours, Thomas and Snuggerud out for 10:52 of their 15:24 at 5-on-5 against Hållander, McDavid and Kapanen (71%, about 31% with no line matching), and they had the worse of the chances, 0.16 to 0.34 expected goals. St. Louis scored one of its five goals then."},{"kind":"match","head":"Holloway’s line drew Draisaitl’s line","text":"Holloway, Buchnevich and Berggren spent 8:54 of their 13:14 at 5-on-5 against Podkolzin, Draisaitl and Joseph (67%, about 33% with no line matching), and they had the worse of the chances, 0.32 to 0.43 expected goals."},{"kind":"match","head":"The third line drew Dickinson’s line","text":"Kaskimäki, McTavish and Dvorský spent 4:47 of their 8:32 at 5-on-5 against Formenton, Dickinson and Dach (56%, about 22% with no line matching)."},{"kind":"swing","head":"One matchup went wrong","text":"Holloway, Buchnevich and Berggren kept drawing Edmonton’s third line, Formenton, Dickinson and Dach. In those 3:02 Edmonton had 0.37 expected goals to St. Louis’s 0.00. Edmonton scored one of its four goals then."},{"kind":"exit","head":"After Jones left, the lines changed but the matchups held","text":"Dach went from 18% to 27% and Podkolzin from 31% to 40% of Edmonton’s 5-on-5 time, and Michaels dropped from 21% to 1%. The matchups stayed: Thomas’s line against Edmonton’s second line (73% before, 62% after) and the third line against Edmonton’s third line (57% before, 55% after)."},{"kind":"result","head":"And it went worse","text":"Edmonton had 2.32 to 1.19 expected goals at 5-on-5 before Jones left and 0.41 to 0.76 after. Edmo